<HelpTab>
    <FluentText>Select a widget in the dashboard designer to change its settings on the right.</FluentText>

    <HelpSection Title="For everyone">
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Greeting</strong>: says hello to whoever is signed in.</li>
            <li><strong>Clock</strong>: 24-hour, date and milliseconds options.</li>
            <li><strong>Text</strong>: your own formatted text, typed in the widget's settings. It's read-only on home
                screens and kiosks, unless you turn on <strong>Can be edited on the kiosk screen</strong>: then a kiosk
                showing it gets an <strong>Edit</strong> button, so staff can update a notice board at the screen itself
                and press <strong>Save</strong>. Turn on <strong>Save automatically as people type</strong> as well, and the
                kiosk shows the text ready to type into, saving a moment after typing stops, with no Edit or Save button.
                While kiosk editing is on, the words belong to the kiosk and are shown read-only in the designer.</li>
            <li><strong>Announcements</strong>: live announcements for the viewer's location, pinned first.</li>
            <li><strong>My Training</strong>: the viewer's own courses.</li>
            <li><strong>My Shifts</strong>: the viewer's upcoming shifts, and optionally time off.</li>
            <li><strong>Who's On Today</strong>: who's working at a location today, and optionally who's clocked in.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="For managers">
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Time Off to Approve</strong>: requests waiting for the viewer.</li>
            <li><strong>Compliance at a Glance</strong>: overdue training and expired or expiring documents.</li>
            <li><strong>Demand and Staffing</strong>: labour hours per game, and the hours most out of line with staffing.
                If your company uses Parties, it also shows the parties, children and party games in the range, and
                hours with a party on are never listed as out of line.</li>
            <li><strong>What's On Today</strong>: today's parties, children and staff on, and the parties still to come. Click
                one to open it, or <strong>View the day</strong> to open <a href="/manage/whats-on">What's On</a>. Select it in the designer
                to set how many to list and, for Admins, which location. Everyone who can see the dashboard sees it, kiosk
                screens included; only Admins and that location's Managers can click through.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Venue technology">
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Laser Game Status</strong> and <strong>Laser Scoreboard</strong>: the current game for a client.
                Turn on <strong>Show past games</strong> in Laser Game Status's settings to list that kiosk's last few
                games under the live status, newest first, and set <strong>How many games</strong> (1 to 20). Each game
                shows when it started, who won, both teams' scores (the winner's in bold) and how many players there
                were. A new game appears as soon as it finishes. The team with the highest total wins, and equal totals
                show <strong>Draw</strong>. If nobody was on a team, the gun with the top score wins. A start time with
                ≈ in front of it is worked out from the game's length, for games played before start times were saved.
                Make the card taller to fit more games; if it's too short, the list scrolls.</li>
            <li><strong>Hall of Fame</strong>: top scores, best accuracy and team totals for a period.</li>
            <li><strong>Playlist picker</strong> and <strong>Now playing</strong>: choose a playlist, see what's
                playing, and skip. Turn on <strong>Show volume and EQ</strong> in Now playing's settings to add the
                kiosk's volume slider and <strong>EQ</strong> button, which work the same as on the Music page.</li>
            <li><strong>Projection Status</strong>: what's showing on a screen, with optional pause, skip and stop. When
                you set it up (and a projection <strong>Button</strong>), the # button beside <strong>Screen</strong> shows
                each screen's number on the kiosk for 8 seconds, so you can pick the right one.</li>
            <li><strong>Live capture</strong>: a kiosk's camera or capture card, live. See <strong>Live capture</strong>
                below.</li>
            <li><strong>Button</strong>: runs a projection program action, such as start, pause or next step. Only
                Admins and Managers can press it.</li>
            <li><strong>Automation Rule Status</strong>: whether a rule is on and when it last ran. Admins can turn it on
                or off.</li>
            <li><strong>Kiosk Health</strong>: which kiosks are online, struggling or offline.</li>
            <li><strong>Operations Alerts</strong>: the open alerts for the locations you manage, with Acknowledge and
                Resolve. Select it in the designer to show only warnings and critical alerts, or hide ones someone has
                acknowledged. On a kiosk dashboard nobody is signed in, so it shows no alerts.</li>
            <li><strong>Checklist Card</strong>: one checklist with its tasks, for a wall screen such as a kiosk. Right-click it
                in the editor to choose the checklist and whether it can be ticked on a kiosk, where ticks are recorded as the
                kiosk. It can hide itself once every task is ticked.</li>
            <li><strong>Checklists Today</strong>: today's checklists where the viewer is working, with how many tasks are done
                and whether each is overdue. Select it in the designer and choose <strong>Widget settings…</strong> to hide
                checklists that are already done. On a kiosk dashboard nobody is signed in, so it asks you to sign in.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Live capture">
        <FluentText>
            Shows a camera or capture card plugged into one of your kiosks, the same picture a projection Live Capture
            step shows, in a tile on any dashboard.
        </FluentText>
        <ol>
            <li>Add <strong>Live capture</strong> from <strong>Kiosks &amp; projection</strong> and select it.</li>
            <li>Pick the camera from <strong>Camera</strong>. Each one is listed as the kiosk's name and then the camera's.</li>
            <li>Turn on <strong>Play the camera's sound</strong> if you want sound as well as the picture.</li>
            <li>Turn on <strong>Fill the tile (crops the edges)</strong> to fill the tile instead of showing the whole picture
                with bars at the sides.</li>
        </ol>
        <FluentText>
            While you're editing, the tile shows the camera's name instead of the picture, so the camera only switches
            on when the dashboard is viewed. The picture appears a few seconds after the dashboard opens, while the
            kiosk starts its camera.
        </FluentText>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>On a kiosk screen</strong>, it plays straight away, with sound if you turned it on. If the camera
                drops out, it keeps trying on its own.</li>
            <li><strong>On a signed-in dashboard</strong>, only Admins and Managers see the picture. Everyone else sees
                "Live capture is for Admins and Managers". Sound starts muted: select the speaker button in the corner
                to hear it. If the picture doesn't start, select <strong>Try again</strong>.</li>
        </ul>
        <HelpNote>
            Nothing is recorded. The camera's kiosk has to be switched on and connected. Watching from outside the venue's
            network may not connect unless your server has a relay (TURN) server set up.
        </HelpNote>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
